From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:13:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] lokql: make scripted runs trustworthy

Running lokql non-interactively (lokql run -f script, CI, graders) could
report success and save the wrong data:

- A query result was pushed to the history only after rendering it, so a
  rendering failure (a chart on a console with no terminal, see below) left
  the previous result as the last one; a following .save wrote that instead.
  Push first, and report a rendering failure as an error.
- Charts are rendered as sixel graphics, which queries the terminal and
  throws when output is redirected. Show the chart's data as a table then.
- .materialize of a failed query replaced the table with an empty one; it
  now refuses with an error.
- A failed .load was only a warning; it is an error now.
- lokql run and convert exit with code 1 when any error was reported. Errors
  are counted by wrapping the explorer's console (ErrorCount), so commands
  and plugins are covered without signature changes.
- Table cells use KustoFormatter.ObjectToKustoString (culture-invariant,
  ISO 8601 datetimes) instead of the current culture's ToString().
- .echo printed only its first word; it prints the whole text.
- Explorer: fix a missing string interpolation in the script load error.
